/node_modules
# Not committed, but `go mod vendor` leaves it here and Go then prefers it
# automatically. So a local build resolves through vendor/ while CI, which
# never has it, resolves through the module cache. Go refuses a vendor tree
# inconsistent with go.mod, so the two cannot silently disagree about versions
# — but they are different code paths, and a vendor/ left behind from an older
# go.mod is worth deleting rather than debugging.
/packages/go/converter/vendor
/packages/ts/*/dist
/packages/ts/*/coverage

/tmp

.devcontainer
.pnpm-store
.npm-cache
.go-cache
.zig-cache
.zig-global-cache
packages/zig/zig-out/
.claude
.buf-cache
.tools
.git-home

.codex/
